SmartCross licensing
====================

SmartCross's own code, documentation and configuration are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal, whose full text is at the end of this
file. This is a learning project.

CC0 covers only the work of SmartCross's authors. Everything listed below belongs
to other people, is not relicensed by this file, and is used under the terms its
owners set. None of it is included in this repository unless marked "included".


Third-party work used by SmartCross
-----------------------------------

Component                 Version      License                 Used for
---------                 -------      -------                 --------
Kenney Car Kit            3.1          CC0 1.0                 Vehicle models (included)
Kenney City Kit Industrial 2.0         CC0 1.0                 Building models (included)
Ursina                    8.3.0        MIT                     3D scene and window
Panda3D                   1.10.16      BSD-3-Clause            Rendering
NumPy                     2.5.4        BSD-3-Clause and others Arrays
Pillow                    13.0.0       MIT-CMU                 Image files
pytest                    9.2.0        MIT                     Tests
Ultralytics               8.3.246      AGPL-3.0-or-later       Vehicle detection and tracking
PyTorch                   2.9.1        BSD-3-Clause            Running the detector
torchvision               0.24.1       BSD-3-Clause            Running the detector
OpenCV (opencv-python)    5.0.0.93     Apache-2.0              Image processing
lap                       0.5.13       BSD-2-Clause            Matching tracks to detections
paho-mqtt                 2.1.0        EPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause MQTT client, used under BSD-3-Clause
Eclipse Mosquitto         2.0.21       EPL-2.0 OR EDL-1.0      Local MQTT broker, run from its Docker image
NVIDIA CUDA libraries     as installed NVIDIA proprietary      GPU support, installed with PyTorch

Other packages are installed automatically by those above and keep their own
licenses, which pip records in each installed package's metadata.

Rights used
-----------

The permissive components above (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, EPL-2.0, EDL-1.0) may be
used, changed and redistributed, including their notices when redistributed. The
NVIDIA libraries may be used under NVIDIA's license and are not redistributed here.

Ultralytics and ultralytics-thop are licensed under the GNU Affero General Public
License. Anyone who distributes SmartCross together with them, or offers it as a
network service, must meet the AGPL-3.0 terms for the combined program, including
providing its source code. CC0 does not remove that obligation, and non-commercial
use is not an exception to it.

Model weights are not part of this repository and are not covered by CC0. Ultralytics
states that models trained with its software fall under AGPL-3.0 by default, so
weights/smartcross_vehicle.pt and yolo11n.pt are treated as AGPL-3.0.

This summary is for convenience. Each component's own license is what applies.


